    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 passing).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec adds an optional `birthDate` to owner creation and a derived read-only `ageBand` on the response. This app serves REST via OfficeFloor function pipelines with MapStruct-mapped DTOs generated from `openapi.yml`, so the change threaded through those layers:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and `ageBand` (readonly string) to the `Owner` response schema. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto.birthDate` and `OwnerDto.ageBand`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter, so the value survives to the later `GET /api/owners/{id}` read the test performs.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 MapStruct auto-maps `birthDate` from request DTO \u2192 entity by name. Added an `ageBand` expression mapping backed by a helper that computes `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` and returns `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+) \u2014 or `null` when no birth date was supplied. It's computed against `registrationDate`, matching how other derived fields (locality, contactPreference) are done.\n\n4. **`db/*/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to all four DB schemas (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) for consistency.\n\nThe test creates an owner with `birthDate=1990-01-01` (registrationDate defaults to today, 2026), reads it back, and asserts `ageBand == \"ADULT\"` (age 36) \u2014 which now passes.",
